            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kaitlin Kuhn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is The Perfect recipe for crunchy fried shrimp! Next time I'll remember to keep the tails on. lol. My family could not get enough of it!! Perfect crunch factor..rated five star!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Valerie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "THE BEST fried shrimp ever! I've eaten lots of fried shrimp in restaurants - and nothing has been better than this! I followed others advice and reduced the salt and omitted the pepper and replaced them with a teaspoon of Old Bay. I also used only two eggs - which was plenty. AND I dipped the shrimp into the egg twice -- once before dredging in flour and then again after dredging in flour (before coating with panko). I also found that one cup of panko was plenty. Another tip -- put them in the freezer for about 10 - 15 minutes after coating and before frying… I do this with everything we fry (makes the batter adhere better). I fried them in 2\" of oil in our deep fryer.",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-21T05:25:00.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sterling Jody Badon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe. The basic concept is perfect and easy to modify to personal likes. \nI used 1/2\" teaspoon of MORTON'S SEASON-ALL and 1/2\" teaspoon of Paul Prudhomme's - SEAFOOD MAGIC instead of salt and pepper. This made the flavor allot better. \nI also made my own bread crumbs using French bread. Just lightly toasted 1/4\" sliced bread at 350DegF. Turned once and cooled then crushed for crumbs. Better than panko.",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-04T03:38:48.897Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brad A"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Regular bread crumbs instead of Panko but loved the crunch. Breading stayed on the shrimp which was a big plus. Let the flour get sticky, then egg wash. Didn’t bread until the flour and egg mixed. Let the breading dry a little before frying. A+ for basic fried shrimp.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-07T02:01:55.720Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CynthiaD"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe, and followed the recipe to the letter. It is OOOOHHH So Good! Crispy and tasty. I prepared my shrimp by removing the shells, but not the tails. Then I patted them very dry with paper towels, so that the dredge and coating would stick. Then I fried in canola oil using my new Presto fryer. My advice...use this recipe. It is excellent. BTW we used Heinz cocktail sauce, and I added extra horseradish for a little spice.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-31T03:13:01.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FriskyCarp5317"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These turned out perfect! I’ve never attempted fried shrimp in all my years of cooking. I guess I assumed it was too much trouble. I followed the recipe as written, used my trusty Fry Daddy, and they were perfect. I don’t think that I cooked them a full minute, maybe 45 seconds, five at a time. Panko is a must! I will definitely be making these again!",
            "datePublished": "2023-08-31T01:18:49.581Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Meghan Vera"
            },
            "reviewBody": "To the flour I added garlic powder, cajun seasoning, and pinch of cayenne pepper. To the eggs I added lemon and lime juice. And to the panko I added salt and paprika. Absolutely delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-16T22:56:16.997Z"
